Third-party notices
-------------------

The plugin bundles MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause, https://maplibre.org) and the
packages MapLibre depends on, plus small runtime helpers from webpack's
style-loader and css-loader (MIT). The build generates the full list, with each
package's license text, as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt in the packaged plugin
(webpack/ThirdPartyNoticesPlugin.ts).

Grafana packages (@grafana/*, React, Emotion) are provided by Grafana at runtime
and are not redistributed with this plugin.

Map data
--------

The default basemap shows OpenStreetMap tiles. Map data © OpenStreetMap
contributors, available under the Open Database License
(https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). The map shows this attribution in
its corner. Tiles come from the OpenStreetMap Foundation's tile servers, whose
usage policy applies: https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/

Basemap presets
---------------

GeoFlow can show basemaps from other providers, picked in the panel options.
The plugin includes none of their data: each map loads from the provider, under
the provider's terms and the plan of the user's own account, and shows the
provider's attribution.

- OpenFreeMap (https://openfreemap.org), terms: https://openfreemap.org/tos/
- Stadia Maps (https://stadiamaps.com), terms:
  https://stadiamaps.com/terms-of-service/
- MapTiler (https://www.maptiler.com), terms:
  https://www.maptiler.com/cloud/terms/. The MapTiler logo is loaded from
  MapTiler and shown as its free plan requires.
- Thunderforest (https://www.thunderforest.com), terms:
  https://www.thunderforest.com/terms/

Their map data is from OpenStreetMap (ODbL) and OpenMapTiles, as each map's
attribution says.
